<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>NATO's Arctic activity poses 'direct threat' to Russia, Lavrov warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d43e2206441b7489dfa413cc9d6f18424b2c25afb76cb3f2916cd65ff0bb8a7f</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T02:40:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-nato-arctic-activity-direct-threat-russia-lavrov" /><summary type="html">Russia views NATO’s growing activity in the Arctic as a direct security threat, Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov said on Monday. NATO launched its Arctic Sentry mission in February to strengthen its presence in the region amid tensions with Moscow and US President Donald Trump’s push to acquire Greenland.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Flash flood in Grand Canyon National Park leaves about 15 missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34625d8187514ad15ac28ce639fbfde46f7c884519cf9ce08ed68a9fcece1808</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T01:38:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-grand-canyon-national-park-flash-flood-missing" /><summary type="html">More than 15 people may be missing after flash floods struck Grand Canyon National Park in Arizona, the National Park Service said on Sunday. Flooding hit the Bright Angel Canyon and Phantom Ranch area on Saturday, prompting authorities to evacuate visitors and search for people who remain unaccounted for.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East Live: US strikes Iran for first time in a month as Tehran retaliates against Jordan base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eee742c97cf77c7c38d78223b9d7d7bcfec0872f523f034a59d65ebb8897a63</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T23:02:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month" /><summary type="html">US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in their first military action in a month on Sunday, breaking a lull in fighting during an intermittent war that has lasted more than six months. Iran swiftly vowed to retaliate for what it called a deadly attack. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US Treasury bars certain journalists from G20 meeting in North Carolina</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ed8ac3a62954e231bb1d19b14cda1021c1ae3425d36c2656634ab76bfff8ad2</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T22:48:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-us-treasury-journalists-from-g20" /><summary type="html">The US Treasury Department denied credentials to reporters from The New York Times, Wall Street Journal and Bloomberg for a Group of 20 finance meeting in North Carolina, the latest restriction on media access under President Donald Trump. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the decision was unrelated to journalists’ viewpoints.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US forces strike Iranian launchers on Larak island in Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85e5e070243a6285a0f90d30bdb777ad834aeeafb37804c41e15df48c732a028</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T20:27:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in the first military action in a month, a US official said Sunday. ⁠Iran's ⁠Revolutionary ​Guards ​said the attack on Larak ​island ‌killed and wounded ⁠several Iranian fighters and ​civilians, and ‌vowed to punish those ​responsible.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says NBC journalist to be reported to FCC for ‘punishment’ over endorsement coverage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c22bc53e9e38530956878f8ac17dbda594884053e9487c0924d6df299e80b070</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T17:06:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-trump-says-nbc-journalist-to-be-reported-to-fcc-for-punishment-over-endorsement-coverage--4b25e5d5d8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-trump-says-nbc-journalist-to-be-reported-to-fcc-for-punishment-over-endorsement-coverage" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday said prominent NBC anchor ​Kristen Welker will be reported to the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) for "rebuke or punishment" after she reported the Republican president had "mixed results" in his endorsement ​of candidates for the November midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>French LGBTQ rights leader hospitalised after ‘despicable homophobic attack’ in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c09c4c70d2a484272580c8855a54c673a38c7d46674361ae880e6e127a535504</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:41:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260830-french-lgbtq-activist-hospitalised-after-despicable-homophobic-attack-in-paris--73c0491ad05b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260830-french-lgbtq-activist-hospitalised-after-despicable-homophobic-attack-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Pierre Picave, a French police officer and head of an LGBTQ rights association, was hospitalised after a nighttime attack in the Marais district in central Paris, prosecutors said Sunday. Paris Mayor Emmanuel Grégoire denounced the "despicable homophobic attack".The suspected attacker has been taken into custody.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Niger junta puts down mutiny with help from Russia's Africa Corps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e763039acab5c90758d93fbaa05ba75067fa13a9b63f112ff6c2ebe191db6661</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:20:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260830-niger-junta-aided-by-russian-paramilitary-forces-regains-control-after-mutiny--b57d1305a2a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260830-niger-junta-aided-by-russian-paramilitary-forces-regains-control-after-mutiny" /><summary type="html">Life returned to normal in Niger's capital on Sunday, a day after mutineers stormed the presidential palace and a military base at Niamey's main airport, resisting forces loyal to the ruling junta until Russia’s Africa Corps intervened. State TV reported that dozens of soldiers were killed or arrested, with some paraded in front of cameras live on television.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>NASA launches new space telescope</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a931b946f9178c0304c764bd2336a45f48cc9de2e05ffdb7baf452b40ed555b</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T14:55:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-nasa-launches-new-space-telescope--6bbfa26cc1e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-nasa-launches-new-space-telescope" /><summary type="html">NASA has successfully launched its newest space telescope from the Kennedy Space Center in Florida. The telescope reached orbit just 10 minutes after liftoff and is now beginning its mission to shed light on some of the universe’s biggest unsolved mysteries. Named after astronomer Nancy Grace Roman, the telescope is being hailed by scientists as a “discovery machine.”</summary></entry><entry><title>Iceland rejects EU accession talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d20f2f18bf51340943e68a3132b4714d34292c8d3f918516fd709d5e5cb0799</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T14:53:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-iceland-rejects-eu-accession-talks--de351b2ef1ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-iceland-rejects-eu-accession-talks" /><summary type="html">Iceland has voted against resuming membership talks with the European Union. The “No” camp won with nearly 53% of the vote, while just over 47% backed the “Yes” side, with only 9,500 votes separating the two. The Nordic island nation is already part of the EU’s single market and the Schengen area, but EU membership would bring it into the bloc’s customs union and pave the way for adopting the euro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Week in pictures: devastating floods in Nepal, death of Dolly Parton and a tornado in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:551d7ee1b374413ad9e58b6589d7920f742e9b9416823774e51e05050da2adf1</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T14:47:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-week-in-pictures-devastating-floods-in-nepal-death-of-dolly-parton-and-a-tornado-in-france--6e7418132498.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-week-in-pictures-devastating-floods-in-nepal-death-of-dolly-parton-and-a-tornado-in-france" /><summary type="html">A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images: a devastating flood tears through Nepal and Tibet, the death of global icon Dolly Parton, a tornado devastates a village in southern France and the Humanoid Robot World Games in China offers a peek at the future.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>France: Far-right and far-left lead polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30ac990f8dec112bdb319aafc863a60e7472830588e8ed41e023afdf661641db</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T14:44:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-far-right-and-far-left-lead-polls--708460084261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-far-right-and-far-left-lead-polls" /><summary type="html">On April 18 and May 2 next year, France will vote to elect a new president to replace Emmanuel Macron. The outgoing president, who has served two terms, cannot run again, while the latest opinion polls are predicting a victory for Marine Le Pen of the far-right National Rally. Although the election is still more than seven months away, several potential candidates have already thrown their hats into the ring and announced their candidacies, including far-left candidate Jean-Luc Mélenchon and former centre-right Prime Minister Édouard Philippe. But do any of them stand a chance of beating the far right? France 24 International Affairs editor Philip Turle shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cyprus: Ferry capsizes with hundreds on board</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5e38e273d7997b628d6528c94396a7eb44bdc8d8d0cd69b7249f0434864431f</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T13:13:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-cyprus-ferry-capsizes-with-hundreds-of-board--500546f52de2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-cyprus-ferry-capsizes-with-hundreds-of-board" /><summary type="html">Authorities say at least six people have died after a catamaran-style ferry carrying 267 passengers and crew capsized off the coast of northern Cyprus. The Turkish ambassador to Nicosia said 172 people had been rescued, with some taken to hospital, while 89 remain missing. The death toll has since risen to seven, according to the latest figures. France 24 correspondent Jasper Mortimer reports the latest from Ankara, Turkey.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Hopes fade for thousands still missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d8fc1b831de1e8e0dbc67ab70f9a4ef6c5d494efca2bb007946204123de69af</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T13:11:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-hopes-fade-for-thousands-still-missing--c75de8c1080d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-hopes-fade-for-thousands-still-missing" /><summary type="html">Four days have passed since catastrophic floods killed more than 750 people. More than 3,000 people are still missing, and hopes of finding survivors are fading. The situation remains concerning, with more heavy rain and flooding expected across the region. France 24 correspondent Shahzaib Wahlah brings us the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Norway’s New King breaks silence after father’s death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80355b2fe0b57154e71e2c7c68b744700fa26aa4e802ddf8630d249454b29bd6</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:31:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-norway-s-new-king-breaks-silence-after-father-s-death--f97ca90ee650.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-norway-s-new-king-breaks-silence-after-father-s-death" /><summary type="html">Norway’s new king addressed the nation for the first time since taking the throne, paying tribute to his 89-year-old father, who died the previous day. Morgan Ayre has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pacific Summit opens amid Taiwan row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6bccc67477bea0bdafef6176d7bb0fc4e1375435572de4e4b79d46b92e5fa1a3</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:29:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pacific-summit-opens-amid-taiwan-row--d0be89950174.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pacific-summit-opens-amid-taiwan-row" /><summary type="html">The annual Pacific Islands Forum begins on Monday in Palau, bringing together the 18-member intergovernmental organisation to discuss regional cooperation and security. On Sunday, Taiwan’s Foreign Minister Lin Chia-lung joined Palau President Surangel Whipps at a ceremony to hand over a fleet of electric buses donated by Taipei. China has criticised Taiwan’s participation in the event. Charles Parton, Senior Associate Fellow at the Royal United Services Institute (RUSI), shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ferry carrying more than 260 people capsizes off northern Cyprus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50a10f3e9304c7decde6fcc898fe4a9463279daa0d9edcfb9267b1c45c5e9bd7</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:27:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ferry-carrying-more-than-260-people-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus--8ab9d00f4329.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ferry-carrying-more-than-260-people-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus" /><summary type="html">Authorities say several people have died after a ferry accident off the coast of northern Cyprus. The catamaran-style vessel was carrying nearly 270 passengers and crew when it capsized. Turkey’s ambassador to Nicosia said many of those on board were rescued, while some were taken to hospital. France 24 correspondent Nathalie Savaricas reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ferry capsizes and sinks off northern Cyprus, killing 8</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27f9201f1cf13b2e03b432910ac55ca2c0867a9fc216afe9a228e36b9b98b602</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:08:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus--feec88e2674e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus" /><summary type="html">At least eight people died when a ferry carrying more than 260 people capsized and sunk off the coast of northern Cyprus on Sunday, according to local authorities. The ship's captain and seven crew members were arrested, said the prime minister of the self-proclaimed Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus (TRNC).</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US and Venezuela seal 25-year oil deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9f87b6465c3b42db8aecc096c8342d79c655af5e4d471eb48573d857c3af6dd</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T11:34:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-and-venezuela-seal-25-year-oil-deal--115b7ac2499b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-venezuela-seal-25-year-oil-deal" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has called it “the biggest oil deal in world history”, while Venezuela’s interim president has assured the public that the country will retain control of its oil under the agreement. The “historic” 25-year deal with Washington involves 65 billion barrels of Venezuelan oil and aims to allow the country to develop its oil industry while preserving “ownership of and sovereignty” over its resources, Rodriguez said in a televised address. Rachael Griffiths has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentines march on Peter Thiel's mansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1078e978107eeab1b5716c4b9557b0533c4148d9d3a2662e7bbc4c2220acbab0</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T10:06:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/argentines-march-on-peter-thiel-s-mansion--3f2016b00340.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-march-on-peter-thiel-s-mansion" /><summary type="html">In Argentina, protesters marched toward a mansion reportedly purchased by American tech billionaire Peter Thiel. Activists accuse Thiel of seeking to profit from the country’s natural resources and wielding excessive political influence in the South American nation. Peter O'Brien reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Thousands still missing as death toll rises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d55885dc106765cdb90e1706728ac8916b3f56d41a8468e3fd2a84b5f9ef9ba1</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T10:04:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises--19b14e275677.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities announced on Sunday that the provisional death toll from the devastating floods had risen to more than 730, with nearly 2,500 people still missing.

Among the thousands of people missing is the husband of a 22-year-old woman, who is still waiting for him to return. Like tens of thousands of Nepalese people in recent days, she went to one of the country’s medical centres to find out whether her husband was among those whose bodies had been recovered in recent days. Caitlin Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Iceland rejects restarting EU accession talks in referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abb20388fa70c690fd4eeed1939baca23929608ab4aa9cb065eab87954db3af2</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:31:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum--6c9761c1e20e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum" /></entry><entry><title>Iceland rejects restarting EU accession talks in referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8cbf2283d28384edc1849775619e32094a97a0b8efbc34a9325296b57d1dd75</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:30:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum--6c9761c1e20e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum" /><summary type="html">Icelanders voted to reject reopening EU membership talks, official results showed Sunday, dealing a blow to the government's push to join the bloc and handing a win to those who argued the country's prized fishing waters were too important to risk. The results will disappoint Brussels, which had hoped to welcome the Nordic country as a new member.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Potter: Versailles turns into wizarding school for a day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b08bab544392b1f02d2cb4c4aa4c7c956ee4a34d45cb889e0d7b6b38899cb8a</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:25:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-harry-potter-versailles-turns-into-wizarding-school-for-a-day--f66120120161.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-harry-potter-versailles-turns-into-wizarding-school-for-a-day" /><summary type="html">Accio nostalgia! ⚡️
 
Can you believe it’s been 25 years since Harry Potter first hit the big screen? To celebrate, French fans turned the Palace of Versailles into Hogwarts for a unique reunion.
 
📹 France 24 was there to capture the magic.</summary></entry></feed>
